:: Pub Gambling Wren Widgets [widget]
<<widget "pubGamblingWrenCheck">>
	<<set _wrenAtRing to false>>
	<<if $xchange.pubGamblingEnabled and !$weekly.gamblingStartupPeriod and ["dusk", "night"].includes(Time.dayState)>>
		<<if !$daily.wrenGamblingRing>>
			<<initBankHeist>>
			<<set _wrenRingChance to ($xchange.bankHeist.landryWarned and !$xchange.bankHeist.wrenRecruited) ? 65 : 35>>
			<<set $daily.wrenGamblingRing to (random(1, 100) lte _wrenRingChance) ? 1 : 2>>
		<</if>>
		<<set _wrenAtRing to $daily.wrenGamblingRing is 1>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

/* The hub of options while sitting with Wren at the ring. */
<<widget "pubGamblingWren">>
	<<bankHeistWrenOptions "gambling">>
	<<if !$daily.wrenDiceTip>>
		<<icon "die.png">><<link [[Ask Wren to read the table (0:10)|Pub Gambling Wren Tip]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Chat (0:30)|Pub Gambling Wren Chat]]>><<pass 30>><<npcincr Wren love 1>><</link>><<glove>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</widget>>

:: Pub Gambling Wren
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "pub">><<effects>><<set $bus to "harvest">>
<<npc Wren>><<person1>>
<<if !$wrenSeen>><<set $wrenSeen to []>><</if>>
<<if $wren_intro is undefined>>
	<<set $wren_intro to true>>
	The <<personsimple>> doesn't look up when you sit down. <<He>> keeps watching the dice as they cross the table,
	then shifts <<his>> attention to the player gathering them for the next throw.
	<br><br>
	"Third throw in a row from the same hand," <<he>> says, without turning towards you.
	"The one in the corner is going to lose everything <<he>> owns tonight."
	The next throw lands, and <<he>> finally looks your way with a small smile.
	<br><br>
	<span class="gold">"Wren,"</span> <<he>> says, offering a hand. "I hear this table is new.
	I like new tables. Nobody's worked out how to cheat at them yet."
<<else>>
	Wren is leaning back in <<his>> chair with a drink <<he>> isn't drinking,
	watching the dice rather than the players.
	<br><br>
	<<if $wrenSeenLast is "bankheist">>
		"Fancy seeing you here, partner," <<he>> says. "Don't worry.
		Nobody at this table listens to anything that isn't a number."
	<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "pregnancy">>
		<<He>> studies your face, then relaxes back into <<his>> chair. "You look better than the last time I saw you."
	<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "prison">>
		"Out and about," <<he>> smirk. "Prison makes people careful. Careful people are terrible gamblers."
	<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "catsuit">>
		"The docks, and now here," <<he>> says. "You do get around."
	<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "gambling">>
		"Back again," <<he>> says. "So am I. Neither of us should be proud of that."
	<<else>>
		"Look who it is," <<he>> says. "Pull up a chair."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<He>> tips <<his>> glass towards the table. "Whoever paid the police to look the other way did a sloppy job of it,
	but I'm not complaining. There's nowhere else in town I can lose money this quickly."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<set $wrenSeen.pushUnique("gambling")>>
<<set $wrenSeenLast to "gambling">>
<<pubGamblingWren>>

:: Pub Gambling Wren Tip
<<effects>>
You ask Wren what <<he>> sees.
<br><br>
<<if !$daily.wrenDiceTip>>
	<<set $daily.wrenDiceTip to true>>
	<<He>> doesn't answer straight away. <<He>> watches two more throws,
	following the shooter's hand from the moment the dice leave <<his>> fingers until they stop.
	Then <<he>> leans closer and lowers <<his>> voice.
	<br><br>
	"Watch the shooter. Before a weak throw, <<he>> lowers one shoulder and releases too early."
	Wren points towards the person collecting the stakes. "That one keeps counting the same money twice.
	If they make a mistake with your bet, make them count it again in front of you."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> taps one of the dice with a fingertip. "These also favour the lower numbers more than they should.
	Keep that in mind before you bet."
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">Wren's read on the table improves your odds at the dice game today.</span>
<<else>>
	"I've told you everything I can see," <<he>> says. "Watching it twice won't change the dice."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<pubGamblingWren>>


:: Pub Gambling Wren Chat
<<effects>>
<<cleareventpool>>
<<addinlineevent "pub_ring_wren_chat_1" 1>>
	Wren nods at the far end of the table, where one of the players is stacking and restacking the same small pile of notes.
	Each time the dice come back, they count the notes again before putting another one on the table.
	<br><br>
	"That one has already lost more than they came in with, and they know it," <<he>> says.
	The player watches another throw, then adds more money to the bet. "They'll stay until somebody makes them leave.
	Every ring has one. It's how the ring pays for itself."
	<br><br>
	<<pubGamblingWren>>
<</addinlineevent>>

<<addinlineevent "pub_ring_wren_chat_2" 1>>
	You ask Wren whether <<he>> ever wins. <<He>> looks down at the notes in front of <<him>>,
	separates a small stack from the rest, then pushes them towards the next bet.
	<br><br>
	"Sometimes," <<he>> says. "I don't come here for the money.
	I come here because people say things at a dice table that they'd never say sober and standing up."
	<<He>> shrugs as the dealer takes the notes. "The money is a fee I pay for listening."
	<br><br>
	<<pubGamblingWren>>
<</addinlineevent>>

<<addinlineevent "pub_ring_wren_chat_3" 1>>
	Wren rolls a die between <<his>> fingers while <<he>> talks, passing it from one hand to the other without looking down.
	A player at the next table cheers over a win, and Wren waits until the shouting settles.
	<br><br>
	"The police know about this room," <<he>> says. "They've known since the first week. That's not a warning
	but just how this works. Stop paying the right people and the police will suddenly decide the gambling bothers them."
	<br><br>
	<<pubGamblingWren>>
<</addinlineevent>>

<<addinlineevent "pub_ring_wren_chat_4" 1>>
	You ask Wren how <<he>> learned to read a table.
	<<He>> catches the die in <<his>> palm and sets it beside <<his>> drink.
	<br><br>
	"Cargo," <<he>> says. "Spend a few years watching customs officers decide which crate to open
	and you learn what people do before they make a choice." <<He>> finally takes a sip from <<his>> drink.
	"Dice are easier than customs officers. They land where they land. People are the ones who lie."
	<br><br>
	<<pubGamblingWren>>
<</addinlineevent>>

<<addinlineevent "pub_ring_wren_chat_5" 1>>
	Wren watches Landry move between the tables, shaking hands and refilling glasses.
	Two players start arguing over a pile of notes, and Landry steps between them before either
	raises their voice much further.
	<br><br>
	After a few quiet words, both sit down again.
	<br><br>
	"<<nnpc_Hes "Landry">> good at this," <<he>> says. "<<nnpc_He "Landry">>
	looks like the least dangerous <<nnpc_gender "Landry">> in any room <<nnpc_hes "Landry">> standing in but can always make people shut.
	That takes work." Wren turns back to you. "Don't tell <<nnpc_him "Landry">> I said anything nice."
	<br><br>
	<<pubGamblingWren>>
<</addinlineevent>>

<<addinlineevent "pub_ring_wren_chat_6" 1>>
	A nervous player across the table keeps rubbing across the edge of a folded note. Wren notices too.
	<br><br>
	"Watch this," <<he>> says quietly. When the next round starts,
	Wren puts down a small bet and looks directly at the nervous player.
	The player hesitate, copy Wren's bet, but then change it and move the money somewhere else.
	<br><br>
	Wren waits until the dice stop before turning back to you. "Didn't matter what I bet.
	People were waiting for somebody else to make the decision first." <<He>> gathers <<his>> own winnings.
	"People who don't trust their own choice are easy to influence."
	<br><br>
	<<pubGamblingWren>>
<</addinlineevent>>

<<addinlineevent "pub_ring_wren_chat_7" 1>>
	A player reaches across the table to collect the winnings. Wren grabs your sleeve before you can move closer.
	<br><br>
	"Left hand," <<he>> says. You watch more carefully as the player gathers the notes with right hand pulls the winnings
	closer, while left one stays near the edge of the pile. The player slide one folded note,
	then move it into the pocket while the other players watch the dice.
	<br><br>
	Wren lets go of your sleeve. "Small theft. That's why it works. Take too much and somebody counts."
	<<He>> watches the player move away from the table. "Take one and everyone assumes they made a mistake counting."
	<br><br>
	<<pubGamblingWren>>
<</addinlineevent>>

<<runeventpool>>
